content.summary_of_the_review:
I would recommend a reject for the following reasons:
1) the results claimed in the abstract, in the introduction and in the list of contributions, are misleading for the reader: they do no reflect the content of the theorems, and their drastic conditions. This is a major issue, since the good faith of the authors could be involved;
2) the formulation of the theorems lacks clarity;
3) the choice of the experimental setup is not explained and looks arbitrary; so, it is impossible to check whether the comparison between setups is fair.

However, I do not contest the proofs, and I believe that the paper is worth publishing if these three issues are addressed.
